<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Firdafylke</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom of the western Norwegian fjords of Sunnfjord and Nordfjord, one of the realms conquered by Harald Fairhair.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Firdafylke, the land of the fjord districts between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sogn">Sogn</a> and Møre, is known almost entirely from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson's</a> sagas. It appears as one of the small coastal kingdoms of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the century before unification.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded beyond the sagas. Its people farmed the narrow fjord valleys and fished the coast, and like neighbouring fylki it had its own assembly. Many families from the district later took part in the settlement of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-iceland">Iceland</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heimskringla">Heimskringla</a>, its king Audbjørn fell fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> at the Battle of Solskjel, and the district then passed under Harald's earls. It became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulating">Gulating</a> law province.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:74.63%;width:2.59%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Norway</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fjordane, Kingdom of Fjordane</dd></dl></aside></div>
